<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Better Traders Guild - Paramedic Mech Medic Duty

    BTG_MechMedic: medbay-anchored medical triage for the Paramedic mech. Tending is
    confined to the mech's MedicalBay (resolved by rect membership in MedicRoomBounds,
    never a radius - so an arbitrarily large or multi-rect medbay works exactly); rescue
    reaches out across the rest of the settlement structure to bring casualties in.

    Priority order:
    1. Tend - patch the worst wounded same-faction defender IN the medbay (worst bleed,
       then lowest health), in a bed or on the floor, using the highest-potency medicine
       in the room. endAfterTendedOnce keeps re-triaging one casualty at a time, and the
       medbay is cleared before the medic walks out to fetch anyone else.
    2. Rescue - carry a downed defender lying anywhere inside the structure footprint -
       including the medbay floor itself - to an unreserved medical bed in the medbay
       (worst-bleed first). No-op when no in-medbay bed is free; floor patients keep
       getting tended where they lie and are promoted into a bed once one frees up.
    3. Floor-rescue (overflow) - when every medbay bed is taken, carry casualties from
       the rest of the structure in anyway and lay them on a clear wall-adjacent,
       non-door-flanking medbay floor cell, where tend/feed reach them and node 2
       later promotes them to a bed. Never fires while a bed is free.
    4. Feed - hand-feed the hungriest DOWNED patient in the medbay (bed or floor), who
       cannot job and would otherwise starve; walking wounded feed themselves via their
       own duty's forage node. Food: the patient's carried rations first, then the best
       in-structure food item, then (urgently hungry) a paste dispenser/VNPE tap. Below
       tend and the rescues so bleeders and retrievals always come first.
    5. Return home - once no medical work remains, walk back into the medbay if an
       out-of-room trip (aborted rescue fetch, longjump) left the mech elsewhere, so
       the idle node below always parks it in its own room.
    6. Idle - dormant self-charge (SelfShutdown, forceSleep off so the LayDown re-check
       wakes it for the next casualty within ~211 ticks).

    Used by: LordJob_MechMedic, assigned via RoomMechLordHelper to the Paramedic mech
    (RoomPart Mech_Paramedic, behavior=Medic).
  -->

  <DutyDef>
    <defName>BTG_MechMedic</defName>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <!-- 1. Stabilize and Tend defenders in the medbay, worst-first (bed or floor), best medicine first. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechMedicTend" />
        <!-- 2. Rescue downed defenders into free hospital beds (fetch from the structure, or promote off the medbay floor). -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechMedicRescue" />
        <!-- 3. Overflow: all beds taken - carry casualties in anyway and lay them on a clear wall-side floor cell. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechMedicFloorRescue" />
        <!-- 4. Feed hungry downed patients in the medbay (they cannot feed themselves). -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechMedicFeed" />
        <!-- 5. No work left: walk back into the medbay before winding down. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechMedicReturnHome" />
        <!-- 6. Idle: dormant self-charge; re-checks ~every 211 ticks to wake for casualties. -->
        <li Class="BetterTradersGuild.AI.Mechs.JobGiver_BTGMechMedicStandby" />
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

</Defs>
